1. DEFINITIONS

"Group" means Archangel, its subsidiaries and affiliated companies, and the
teams and personnel (including contractors working under their direction)
acting on their behalf.

"Design System" means the Handcrafted Design System, consisting of the
files in the styles/ and design/ directories of this repository (and as
served from https://static.wearearchangel.com/styles/ and
https://static.wearearchangel.com/design/), including its stylesheets,
design tokens, components, documentation and source code, together with the
Starter Assets, but excluding Third-Party Components. Other files in this
repository, including fonts/, are not part of the Design System.

"Starter Assets" means the files in the manifest/ directory and the files
named placeholder.* at the root of this repository (and as served from
https://static.wearearchangel.com/manifest/ and
https://static.wearearchangel.com/placeholder.*). They are placeholder
icons, images, media and documents that are meant to be used as a starting
point and replaced.

"Third-Party Components" means the materials identified in the
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md file at the repository root and in fonts/OFL.txt,
which are licensed to you by their own authors under their own terms.
Where a file in the Design System is derived from a Third-Party Component,
this Agreement applies only to Archangel's own contributions to that file.

"Client" means a person or organisation for which a member of the Group
creates a Deliverable.

"Deliverable" means any website, application, product, document or other work
that incorporates or is built with the Design System and is created by a
member of the Group either for a Client or for the Group's own internal or
proprietary use.


2. LICENSE GRANT

Subject to this Agreement, Archangel grants each member of the Group
a limited, worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive and non-transferable
license to:

(a) use and reproduce the Design System;
(b) modify the Design System and create derivative works of it; and
(c) incorporate the Design System, and derivative works of it, into
    Deliverables, and host, deliver and distribute those Deliverables.

Starter Assets. You may use, copy, modify and replace the Starter Assets,
include them in Deliverables, and ship them to end users (for example as
default or fallback content). A Deliverable may also load them at runtime
from https://static.wearearchangel.com/. Archangel may change, rename or
remove Starter Assets, or stop serving them, at any time and without notice,
and does not promise that any file path will stay available. If a
Deliverable needs a Starter Asset to remain available, copy the file into
the Deliverable. Files you create to replace Starter Assets are not part of
the Design System and belong to you or your Client.


3. DELIVERABLES AND CLIENTS

A member of the Group may grant a Client a sublicense to use, host
and maintain the Design System, and modify it for that purpose, only as
incorporated in the Deliverable (including where the Deliverable loads
Starter Assets at runtime under Section 2) and only for the Client's own
business use of that Deliverable.

A Client has no right to extract the Design System from the Deliverable,
distribute it separately, or use it to build products or services for third
parties other than through the Deliverable itself.

A sublicense granted under this Section for a Deliverable delivered before
this Agreement ends continues for that Deliverable.


